{
  "mappings": [
    {
      "name": "initialize accepted (201, pending) -- only with both keys and the documented body",
      "priority": 10,
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "urlPath": "/payments",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        },
        "bodyPatterns": [
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.reference",
              "matches": "^[0-9a-f-]{36}$"
            }
          },
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.currency",
              "equalTo": "XAF"
            }
          },
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.phone",
              "matches": "^\\+237[0-9]{9}$"
            }
          },
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": "$[?(@.amount >= 100)]"
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 201,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":201,\"status\":\"Created\",\"message\":\"Payment initialized\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"{{jsonPath request.body '$.reference'}}\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": [
          "Transcribed from openapi.yaml 2.1.0's initializePayment (201) and NOT from Notch Pay: nothing in",
          "this repository has called Notch Pay. Matching on X-Grant is a CONTRACT of this stub, not a",
          "claim about Notch Pay, whose specification asks only for Authorization here: ADR-0031",
          "condition 1 says the private key rides on every call, and an adapter that stopped sending it",
          "matches no mapping and gets WireMock's 404, which it reads as Config. The body pattern holds",
          "RFC-0012 section 3's shape: our reference, XAF, a +-prefixed Cameroonian number, and an",
          "amount at or above Notch Pay's documented minimum of 100."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize: the account's keys refused (401)",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "urlPath": "/payments",
        "headers": {
          "Authorization": {
            "equalTo": "bad-key"
          }
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 401,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "jsonBody": {
          "code": 401,
          "status": "Unauthorized",
          "message": "Unauthenticated."
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "The value the conformance suite's Credentials::Rejected sends. The adapter must page (provider_account_blocked), never report a payer's problem. Notch Pay's exact 401 message is not documented; the adapter does not read it."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize: a payment with this reference already exists (409)",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "urlPath": "/payments",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        },
        "bodyPatterns": [
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.reference",
              "equalTo": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000dd"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 409,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "jsonBody": {
          "code": 409,
          "status": "Conflict",
          "message": "A payment with this reference already exists"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": [
          "REF_DUPLICATE. From Notch Pay's errors page; ABSENT from openapi.yaml 2.1.0 (RFC-0012 section 10",
          "item 4). The adapter reads the payment (the retrieve catch-all answers complete) and reports",
          "Submitted with no key material: the crash-retry case."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "initialize: a redirect, which must never be followed",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "urlPath": "/payments",
        "headers": {
          "X-Grant": {
            "matches": ".+"
          },
          "Authorization": {
            "matches": ".+"
          }
        },
        "bodyPatterns": [
          {
            "matchesJsonPath": {
              "expression": "$.reference",
              "equalTo": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000302"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 307,
        "headers": {
          "Location": "/__never-followed/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000302"
        }
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "REF_REDIRECT. A followed 307 replays the body (the payer's number) and every header reqwest does not strip, X-Grant among them."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the redirect's target, answering 'accepted' so a followed redirect would be an Ok",
      "priority": 1,
      "request": {
        "urlPath": "/__never-followed/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000302"
      },
      "response": {
        "status": 201,
        "headers": {
          "Content-Type": "application/json"
        },
        "body": "{\"code\":201,\"status\":\"Created\",\"message\":\"Payment initialized\",\"transaction\":{\"id\":\"pay.test_{{randomValue length=12 type='ALPHANUMERIC'}}\",\"reference\":\"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000302\",\"amount\":5000,\"currency\":\"XAF\",\"status\":\"pending\"}}"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "why": "redirects_are_refused_and_never_followed asserts the journal never shows this path."
      }
    }
  ]
}
